From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:12:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: TVB: make growth refusals visible

At a refused growth request the firmware only re-requests, about every
355 ms, until pages free up: renders crawl and a client's exit drains for
minutes, which looked like a hang (2026-10-24 analysis, tvb-cap-* kits).
Record why each request was refused (at tvb_max_blocks, render arena VA
full, or a failed non-reclaiming allocation), count refusals by reason in
dep_stats (tvb_refused_cap/_va/_memory, summing to tvb_refused), and warn
for the first refusal of the boot with its reason; later pools are
reported at info, since CTS performance cases refuse growth in every
process. No growth, cap or VA change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
